    "status_change_narrative": "",
    "data_gaps_followups": [
      "GAP 1 – APR/APOR CONTRADICTION (CRITICAL): The structured APR (8.12%) and APOR (7.02%) produce a 1.10% spread inconsistent with the HMDA-reported rate spread of 2.37%. WHY IT MATTERS: The HPML classification and all associated obligations depend on whether the APR exceeds APOR by 1.50 percentage points. An error in either direction creates regulatory exposure. MINIMUM ACCEPTABLE EVIDENCE: APR calculation worksheet showing all finance charges and APR computation; FFIEC APOR weekly table for the week containing April 10, 2024 for a 30-year fixed-rate first-lien product; HMDA rate spread calculation documentation. RECOMMENDED ACTION: Obtain and review the APR worksheet from the LOS; pull and retain the specific FFIEC APOR table page for the lock-date week; reconcile with the HMDA rate spread; correct any erroneous filed data.",
