      "GAP 5 – ADDITIONAL APPRAISAL (FLIP RULE) ANALYSIS NOT DOCUMENTED: The file states additional_appraisal_required = false but contains no supporting analysis. WHY IT MATTERS: 12 CFR § 1026.35(c)(4) requires creditors to evaluate whether the seller acquired the property within 180 days and whether a price increase threshold is met. Undocumented conclusions are not examination-ready. MINIMUM ACCEPTABLE EVIDENCE: Prior sale history from title search or county records showing seller acquisition date; documented analysis of whether the flip-rule thresholds are triggered; if thresholds not met, a written conclusion in the file. RECOMMENDED ACTION: Review title commitment for prior sale date; document the flip-rule analysis in the credit or compliance file.",
